# ---------------------------------------------------------
# .dockerignore is a SECURITY CONTROL, not an optimisation.
#
# Everything not excluded here is sent to the Docker daemon and
# baked into an image layer by `COPY . .`. Image layers are
# PERMANENT: deleting a file in a later layer does not remove it
# from the earlier one, and anyone who can pull the image can read
# it back out.
#
# This repository's root currently holds .env, credentials.json,
# token.json and google_calendar_token.json - a complete set of live
# OAuth credentials. Without the block below, `docker push` publishes
# them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------

# --- secrets: the reason this file exists ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
credentials.json
token.json
*token*.json
*_token.json
google_calendar_token.json

# --- history: .git carries every secret ever committed, even ones
#     since deleted from the working tree ---
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- host-built virtualenv: Linux-incompatible binaries, and huge ---
.venv
venv

# --- build noise ---
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
*.egg-info

# --- the frontend builds in its own image; node_modules from the host
#     contains platform-specific binaries that break in the container ---
frontend/node_modules
frontend/.next
frontend/.next-e2e
frontend/test-results
frontend/playwright-report

# --- not needed at runtime ---
tests
phases_doc
devloper_docs
*.md
!README.md
scripts/check_secrets.py
jj.txt
